From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: paranoica <mitjumper@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(workspace): keep the global active workspace on the
 monitor in use

New windows and launch contexts start on the global active workspace, which per-monitor activation never updated. A window opening on the monitor that owned the stale workspace stayed on it instead of the workspace shown there.
---
 src/core/workspace.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/workspace.c b/src/core/workspace.c
index 11e2763..60b722e 100644
--- a/src/core/workspace.c
+++ b/src/core/workspace.c
@@ -650,6 +650,9 @@ meta_workspace_activate_with_focus (MetaWorkspace *workspace,
       /* Update monitor workspace container */
       container->active_workspace = workspace;
 
+      workspace->manager->active_workspace = workspace;
+      g_signal_emit_by_name (workspace->manager, "active-workspace-changed");
+
       g_object_notify_by_pspec (G_OBJECT (workspace), obj_props[PROP_ACTIVE]);
       if (old_workspace)
         g_object_notify_by_pspec (G_OBJECT (old_workspace), obj_props[PROP_ACTIVE]);
